Install and check

bash
sudo apt-get install -y pass
pass --version

2. Initialize the store with Alice's GPG key from part b

bash
pass init "alice@example.com.invalid"

This creates ~/.password-store. Your own generated key has "ultimate" trust, which pass requires.

3. Add a generated password (shows the generator)

bash
pass generate demo/example.com 20

4. Add a password manually

bash
pass insert demo/mail-demo

5. List and retrieve

bash
pass ls
pass show demo/example.com

The GPG passphrase prompt appears when you retrieve. That prompt is your demonstration of the master secret.

6. Edit an entry (add a username line)

bash
pass edit demo/mail-demo

7. Show that the files really are encrypted

bash
ls -R ~/.password-store
cat ~/.password-store/demo/example.com.gpg | head -c 100
gpg --list-packets ~/.password-store/demo/example.com.gpg | head -20

The .gpg file is unreadable, and the packet listing shows it is encrypted to Alice's public key.

8. Optional: version history with git

bash
pass git init
pass git log

9. Optional: remove a test entry

bash
pass rm demo/mail-demo

