Attacks that exploit people who don't use password managers

When people don't have a manager to help them, they will use the same password, make a memorable and guessable password, and manually enter the password into a page.

Attacks that exploit people who don't use password managers

Without a manager, people tend to reuse passwords, choose memorable and guessable ones, and type them into pages by hand.

